---
term: Jurisdiction
section: jurisdiction-and-resources
order: 10
definition: The scope of matters, resources, and people over which a charter gives a corporation authority.
seeAlso:
  - commons
  - delegated-public-authority
---
Jurisdiction isn't the same as territory. It comes from three sources:

- [[Ownership]] held by constituents
- Authority delegated or commissioned by a parent
- [[Asset|Assets]] or common resources that members contribute

[[Territorial jurisdiction]] is only one type of jurisdiction among many.
